From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Subject: [PATCH] Migrate 0413-white-03-amd-shader-fixes.patch

Source: 0413-white-03-amd-shader-fixes.patch
accesses and NaN-defined min/max

Port of mja00/Lichii c418e4f477 and 5e8d409f81 (misaligned vector reads) and 913ba475da
(NaN-defined min, max, clamp), also in chuppatricky/Lichii as 39cdadb495 and 92d8eec98b (v13).
Storage buffers bind at the device's storage buffer alignment, 4 bytes on RADV, so an aligned
8 or 16-byte guest access can sit at any word of its binding: the vector view (offset >> shift)
then reads the vector before it and shifts every component by one or more words. In Ocarina of
Time that fed wrong words and NaN into the lighting (green lighting, cyan sky, overbright light
in the reports); mja00 restored the Maxwell FMNMX/.SAT NaN rule once the reads were right. The
PS5 runs RADV with the same 4-byte alignment and T26 lacks all three.

EDEN_NX2_AMD_SHADER_FIXES=1, read once by the SPIR-V backend:
- global memory loads and stores of 8 and 16 bytes find their buffer once and go word by word
  through the U32 view when the alignment is below the access size (DefineGlobalMemoryFunctions);
- storage buffer loads and stores of 64 and 128 bits take the vector view only for an immediate
  offset that is a multiple of the size, or when the alignment covers it, otherwise 32-bit loads
  (VectorViewIsExact);
- FPMin/FPMax 32 and 64 and Clamp (saturate, FPClamp 16/32) use OpNMin/OpNMax.
Unset, every path is as before. Shaders are translated at every boot, so env.txt is enough.
Differences from the sources: ours is behind the switch; Lichii's non-aliasing word path (calls
per word) is not in our tree and is not added; Lichii's conditions otherwise kept.

Not built, not run. Clang syntax check clean on the three sources.

